  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between K-252a and GTPase KRas through the compound Theasaponin E1, which acts as a target of multiple proteins encoded by K-252a. Specifically, K-252a is associated with two distinct targets, Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1 and Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 3A1, both of which are also targets of Theasaponin E1. These targets are further linked to GTPase KRas, indicating a possible pathway through which Theasaponin E1 may influence GTPase KRas activity. The scores for these relationships are consistent across different paths, suggesting a reliable connection. The mechanism likely involves Theasaponin E1 modulating the activity of these transporters, which in turn may affect the downstream signaling of GTPase KRas. While the evidence is robust, the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated."
